@startuml
title Class Diagram - Canopée (Real-Time Messaging)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<planned>> White
  BorderColor<<planned>> Gray
  FontColor<<planned>> Gray
}

' ============================
' Implemented classes
' ============================

class User <<Django built-in>> {
  +id : Integer
  +username : String {unique}
  -password : String {hashed}
  +is_active : Boolean
}

class Conversation {
  +id : Integer
  +is_group : Boolean = false
  +name : String [0..100]
  +created_at : DateTime
}

class Message {
  +id : Integer
  +content : String
  +created_at : DateTime
}

' ============================
' Planned class (not in the code yet)
' ============================

class Membership <<planned>> {
  +joined_at : DateTime
  +last_read_at : DateTime
}

' ============================
' Associations
' ============================

User "2..* participants" -- "0..* conversations" Conversation : participates in >
Conversation "1 conversation" *-- "0..* messages" Message : contains >
User "1 author" -- "0..* messages" Message : writes >

(User, Conversation) .. Membership

' ============================
' Notes
' ============================

note right of Conversation
  Private conversation: is_group = false,
  exactly 2 participants, no name,
  only one per pair of users.
  Group: is_group = true, optional name.
  is_group is set by the server, never by the client.
end note

note bottom of Message
  Django mapping:
  author = ForeignKey(User, on_delete=CASCADE)
  conversation = ForeignKey(Conversation, on_delete=CASCADE)
  Deleting a conversation deletes its messages.
end note

note left of User
  Account deletion is a soft delete:
  is_active = false and an unusable password.
  The user's messages stay visible.
end note

note bottom of Membership
  <<planned>> association class for a
  persistent unread counter. Today the relation
  is a plain participants = ManyToManyField(User);
  Django can migrate it to a through= model.
end note

@enduml
